# Cloudflare Pages only. GitHub Pages and serve.py ignore this file entirely.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. Cloudflare Pages "cleans" URLs by default: a request for
# /app.html gets a 308 to /app. That quietly breaks the installed PWA, and it
# breaks it in the least obvious way possible:
#
#   manifest.webmanifest declares  start_url: ./app.html
#   sw.js precaches                ./app.html  (and the four other pages)
#
# so the launch redirects to /app, the service worker looks for /app in the
# cache, does not find it — it cached /app.html — and falls through to its
# navigate fallback, which serves index.html. The result is that opening the
# installed app offline lands you on the marketing page. Nothing errors.
#
# A 200 here is a REWRITE, not a redirect. The target must NOT be the same path:
# path directly and never runs the .html-stripping step, so /app.html stays a
# real 200 and every cache key, the start_url and the navigate fallback keep
# agreeing with each other.
#
# One line per page in app/. Adding a new .html page means adding a line here —
# test/test_redirects.js fails if you forget.

/index.html    /            200
/app.html      /app         200
/legal.html    /legal       200
/compare.html  /compare     200
/404.html      /404         200
